# A guide page for each tale of the Mabinogion (mabinogi-<id>.html), November 2026.
# Each guide gives the facts at a glance, the whole tale part by part, its people (person pages, src/mabinogi_people.py)
# and its places in Wales on a numbered map. The retellings to read aloud stay on the legend pages (legend-*.html).
# Ifan asked for "a lot of information about the Mabinogi" (12 November 2026).
# House rules (EDITORIAL.md): proud and respectful; the Britons and the Cymry, never Celts; Arthur is a king.
# The tales are told in their own words ("the tale tells"), as Welsh tradition has kept them.
# Sources: Ifor Williams, Pedeir Keinc y Mabinogi (1930); Sioned Davies, The Mabinogion (2007);
# Rachel Bromwich, Trioedd Ynys Prydein; Hywel Wyn Owen and Richard Morgan, Dictionary of the Place-Names of Wales (2007).
# Place positions are for the map only: where a place of the tale is not known for certain, the pin marks
# the place that tradition or the name points to, and the note says so.
#
# Tale: id, group, n (its label), cy (the Welsh title), en, legend (the retelling, or ""), era (colour), pic (gallery id),
# sumEn/sumCy, pEn/pCy (prose: "## " heading, "|| a | b" fact row, "> quote | source"), people [slugs],
# places [(en, cy, lat, lon, note EN, note CY, link or "")]; lat None = not on the map of Wales.

# Pictures shown with each guide ("figs"): Commons files with their credits, as lit_fig() in build.py takes them:
# (file, author, licence, licence URL, caption EN, caption CY, width, height). tools/fetch_photos.py keeps them on the site.
