    ("Caer Dathyl, Arfon", "Caer Dathyl, Arfon", None, None, "Math’s court. Its place is not known for certain; tradition looks for it in Arfon, between the Menai and the mountains.", "Llys Math. Nid yw’n hysbys i sicrwydd ble roedd; mae traddodiad yn chwilio amdano yn Arfon, rhwng y Fenai a’r mynyddoedd.", ""),
    ("Rhuddlan Teifi", "Rhuddlan Teifi", 52.045, -4.24, "Pryderi’s court in Ceredigion, by the Teifi near Llanybydder, where Gwydion told his tales and took the swine.", "Llys Pryderi yng Ngheredigion, ger y Teifi yn ymyl Llanybydder, lle adroddodd Gwydion ei chwedlau a chymryd y moch.", ""),
    ("Elenydd", "Elenydd", 52.29, -3.73, "The high moorland of the Cambrian Mountains, the first stage of the swine’s road north.", "Rhostir uchel Elenydd, cam cyntaf ffordd y moch tua’r gogledd.", ""),
    ("Mochdref, between Ceri and Arwystli", "Mochdref, rhwng Ceri ac Arwystli", 52.5, -3.37, "Mochdre near Newtown, Powys: ‘swine town’, named, the tale says, for a night the herd rested there.", "Mochdre ger y Drenewydd, Powys: ‘tref y moch’, a enwyd, medd y chwedl, am noson y gorffwysodd y gyr yno.", ""),
    ("Mochnant", "Mochnant", 52.825, -3.3, "‘Swine stream’ in Powys, around Llanrhaeadr-ym-Mochnant, another night on the road.", "‘Nant y moch’ ym Mhowys, o gwmpas Llanrhaeadr-ym-Mochnant, noson arall ar y daith.", "place-llanrhaeadr.html"),
    ("Mochdre in Rhos", "Mochdre yn Rhos", 53.295, -3.77, "Mochdre near Colwyn Bay, the last swine town before Arfon.", "Mochdre ger Bae Colwyn, y dref foch olaf cyn Arfon.", ""),
    ("Dinas Dinlle and Caer Arianrhod", "Dinas Dinlle a Chaer Arianrhod", 53.082, -4.335, "The hillfort of Dinas Dinlle on the shore of Arfon bears Lleu’s name. Off the coast, a reef seen at low tide is still called Caer Arianrhod.", "Mae bryngaer Dinas Dinlle ar lan Arfon yn dwyn enw Lleu. Oddi ar yr arfordir, gelwir craig a welir ar drai yn Gaer Arianrhod o hyd.", ""),
    ("Pennardd and Coed Alun", "Pennardd a Choed Alun", 53.02, -4.37, "The two maenors in Arfon, near Clynnog, between which Math’s army fought Pryderi.", "Y ddwy faenor yn Arfon, ger Clynnog, y bu byddin Math yn ymladd â Phryderi rhyngddynt.", ""),
    ("Nantlle", "Nantlle", 53.05, -4.22, "Nantlleu, Lleu’s valley, where Gwydion found the eagle in the oak between two lakes.", "Nantlleu, cwm Lleu, lle cafodd Gwydion yr eryr yn y dderwen rhwng dau lyn.", ""),
    ("Dôl Benmaen", "Dôl Benmaen", 52.94, -4.17, "Near Penmorfa, where Pryderi made his last stand and offered to settle the war in single combat.", "Ger Penmorfa, lle safodd Pryderi am y tro olaf a chynnig setlo’r rhyfel mewn ymladdfa un-ac-un.", ""),
    ("Maentwrog and Y Felenrhyd", "Maentwrog a’r Felenrhyd", 52.945, -3.99, "Pryderi fell at Y Felenrhyd on the Dwyryd and was buried at Maentwrog. ‘And there is his grave.’", "Syrthiodd Pryderi yn y Felenrhyd ar afon Dwyryd a’i gladdu ym Maentwrog. ‘Ac yno y mae ei fedd.’", ""),
    ("Mur Castell (Tomen y Mur)", "Mur Castell (Tomen y Mur)", 52.932, -3.925, "Lleu’s court in Ardudwy: the Roman fort of Tomen y Mur, high above Trawsfynydd.", "Llys Lleu yn Ardudwy: caer Rufeinig Tomen y Mur, yn uchel uwchben Trawsfynydd.", ""),
    ("Llech Ronw and the Cynfal", "Llech Ronw ac afon Cynfal", 52.957, -3.9, "On the bank of the Cynfal below Ffestiniog, where Gronw killed the stag, and where he held up the stone against Lleu’s spear.", "Ar lan afon Cynfal islaw Ffestiniog, lle lladdodd Gronw’r carw, a lle daliodd y llech rhyngddo a gwaywffon Lleu.", ""),
    ("Llyn y Morwynion", "Llyn y Morwynion", 52.975, -3.875, "The lake on the moor above Ffestiniog where Blodeuwedd’s maidens drowned as they fled.", "Y llyn ar y rhos uwchben Ffestiniog lle boddodd morynion Blodeuwedd wrth ffoi.", ""),
